 - The bugs Claude found were mostly ones that hadn't run yet: Python only fails on a line when it executes it. Running the tests after each small change catches them sooner.
 - **To do:** rewrite `cli.py` and `tests/test_cli.py` from memory without AI, since Claude wrote most of the final version of that layer.
+
+## 2026-11-18: `list --category`
+
+Tool: Claude Code in the terminal. I asked it to add the feature and tests, and it wrote all of it.
+
+### What the AI did
+
+- Added an optional `category` argument to `ExpenseStore.list_all`. The filter runs in SQL (`WHERE ? IS NULL OR category = ?`), so no category still means "list everything".
+- Added `--category` to the `list` subcommand, plus a separate "No expenses in category 'x'." message when nothing matches.
+- Wrote four tests: two in `tests/test_storage.py` (filter works, unknown category is empty) and two in `tests/test_cli.py` (only that category is printed, the no-match message).
+- Added the new command to the README usage block.
+
+### How the output was checked
+
+- `uv run pytest` (34 passed), `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run mypy .` (strict), all clean.
+
+### Notes
+
+- Matching is exact and case-sensitive (`Food` is not `food`), the same as how `summary` groups categories.
